# Shadowgain 124: pin LF on everything that is EXECUTED, not just read.
#
# The repo root sets `* text=auto`, and this machine has core.autocrlf=true. Together those
# store LF and check out CRLF on Windows - which is fine for C# and fine for anything only ever
# opened in an editor, and NOT fine for these:
#
#   *.sh              run in Git Bash locally, and shipped to the droplet. A `#!/usr/bin/env
#                     bash\r` shebang fails with "bad interpreter: no such file or directory",
#                     and every heredoc terminator gains an invisible \r that stops matching.
#   *.service         systemd parses CRLF unit files as values with trailing \r - an ExecStart
#                     path that then does not exist.
#   Caddyfile*        the caddyfile adapter is whitespace-sensitive.
#   *.sql             piped into `mysql` over ssh.
#
# The failure mode all four share is that the file looks perfect in an editor and breaks only on
# the machine it was shipped to. Pinning them costs nothing and removes the class.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf
Caddyfile*  text eol=lf

# Generated icon PNGs - binary, never diffed, never munged.
*.png       binary
